      "ask": "Correct process lists fail tests: This assertion assumes the newly launched process is pytest's first child.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/reflex_base/utils/test_processes.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "`stop_process_tree` abandons descendants as soon as the root is reaped, so a SIGTERM-responsive wrapper can leave its still-running frontend orphaned. Capture the tree before forwarding the first signal, or retain an equivalent process-group/tree snapshot for the later forced cleanup.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "A batch already inside `_write_all` stays unsplit when shutdown begins, so the drain can exit with a truncated JSON record. Make an in-flight batch interruptible or write records individually.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/log.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "`_alive` reports zombie descendants as alive because `os.kill(pid, 0)` succeeds for them. In environments where orphans are not reaped, every stop waits the full timeout for processes that already exited. Check `/proc/ /stat` for state `Z` on Linux, or treat zombies as gone.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "The docstring promises that descendants started during the wait are caught before the kill, but the re-scan runs only while the root is still alive. When the root exits during the wait, children it already spawned can start new processes that are never signalled. Either narrow the docstring or snapshot the tree again before the root exits.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "A signal that arrives during the frontend shutdown wait aborts `stop_process_tree` before its SIGKILL step. The handler only suppresses repeats after a first signal, so this first signal raises out of the cleanup. Consider making the handler ignore signals once cleanup has begun, or running the frontend stop outside the signal-raising window.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "Windows bypasses the new signal guard, so a second Ctrl-C can still raise `KeyboardInterrupt` during `stop_frontend` cleanup. Install an ignore-repeat `SIGINT` handler on Windows too.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
