      "ask": "`select.PIPE_BUF` is Unix-only, so `_atomic_chunks` raises AttributeError on Windows as soon as a batch has two records. That error escapes the `OSError` suppression, kills the reader thread, and can leave the supervised command blocked on a full pipe. Guard the attribute with a fallback, such as `getattr(select, \"PIPE_BUF\", 4096)`, or define the constant once at module level.",
