    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "This test asserts nothing, so it passes even if the pump stops reading after the consumer disappears. Add an assertion that the child pipe reached EOF, or check that the pump consumed the written bytes, e.g. by checking `pump.idle_since` or the pipe state after `run()`.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/reflex_base/utils/test_supervisor.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "Forced exit leaves servers running: If `npm` exits on SIGTERM but its server ignores SIGTERM, `stop_process_tree` saves the server's PID for the five-second wait and eventual SIGKILL.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "Forced exit blocks on output: If a plain run has stderr redirected to a full pipe whose consumer stopped reading, this `os.write` blocks before the handler can kill children or exit.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "`proc.stdout.readline()` has no timeout, so if the child never prints the helper PID (for example, the first signal stops being handled), this test blocks the suite instead of failing. Read stdout with a deadline, such as `select` on the pipe, or poll with `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT` as the other subprocess tests here do.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/test_reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "On Windows this makes the forced-exit path a no-op for descendants. `os._exit` then leaves the frontend tree running whenever the stuck cleanup is not inside `stop_process_tree`. The docstring's justification only holds if `taskkill` already ran. Either make the Windows branch end the tree, or document that forced exit does not stop descendants on Windows.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "The forced-shutdown path can fail before killing descendants: `os.write(2, ...)` raises for a closed stderr or blocks on a full, unread pipe. Make this diagnostic best-effort and nonblocking, then always run `kill_descendants` and `_exit`.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "This test keeps the root alive, so the killed grandchild stays a zombie under it. `_alive` only detects zombies on Linux, so on macOS/BSD the test will wait out the 1 s timeout and fail. Skip it off Linux, or check for zombies with `ps` on other POSIX systems.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/reflex_base/utils/test_process_tree.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "ask": "Acknowledge the earlier unrelated CodSpeed regression only if its red mark blocks review; the current head no longer carries that failure.",
      "addressed": true
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "Forced exit kills unrelated tasks: saved process IDs must be checked before SIGKILL so a reused PID cannot target an unrelated process.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "The forced exit SIGKILLs every PID recorded when cleanup began without checking process identity; validate identity before signaling.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/reflex.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "`kill_descendants` stores raw PIDs for a potentially long cleanup and must avoid signaling an unrelated process after PID reuse.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/utils/process_tree.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "The recorded-PID tests use pytest itself as the root and can kill unrelated test-runner descendants; give each test a dedicated root process.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/reflex_base/utils/test_process_tree.py",
      "outdated": true
    }
  ],
